Then in the deals section reference each item once or note \"covered above\" \u2014 never repeat the same item twice in the report.\n4. COMPLETENESS GATE \u2014 After writing the report, verify that every AI-RELEVANT item from RESEARCH DATA fresher than 14 days appears in exactly one section. Dropping irrelevant items is required, not optional.\n5. FACTUAL/NEWS BULLETS \u2014 every factual or news bullet item must end with a one-line reason it matters AND a source URL. Final-summary status lines and the exact no-promotion fallback are explicitly exempt from this URL requirement. Format: \"- **Title** \u2014 one-line why it matters \u2014 <url>\". No bare links without context; no bullets without links.\n6. NO FILLER \u2014 never pad with placeholders or generic copy. If a section has fewer than 3 items, still include what exists \u2014 do not skip the section entirely. For the deals section use the exact fallback below.\n7. PRICING FORMAT \u2014 all pricing = $ per million tokens ($/1M). Never use raw decimals.\n8. \"Best Local Model\" = specific model name only (e.g. Llama 3.3 70B, Phi-4, Qwen3-235B). NEVER a tool/app (LM Studio, Ollama, Jan). Leave blank if no notable local model today.\n9. \"Featured Models\" = tag EVERY model mentioned anywhere in the report.\n10. Importance: Critical=frontier model released OR major security issue. High=significant model/pricing. Medium=updates. Low=minor.\n11. Source URLs = copy verbatim from RESEARCH DATA. Never construct URLs.\n12. Use ## for sections, **bold** for key terms, bullet points for lists. NO markdown tables in the body.\n13. \"Summary\" property = max 280 characters, plain text only, and it should mention the top deal if one exists.\n14. The \"\uD83D\uDD25 AI Deals, Pricing & Launch Intelligence\" section must use ONLY facts from DEALS & LAUNCH INTELLIGENCE DATA above \u2014 never training-memory pricing, discounts, or promotions for this section.\n15. Never invent prices, dates, percentages, links, or availability for any deal. If a field is unknown, write \"Unknown\".\n16. METADATA CONSISTENCY \u2014 the JSON block and the body MUST agree: new_model_released=true only if \"New Model Releases\" lists a release; pricing_changed=true only if a price actually changed; open_source=true only if an open-source project is covered; free_promotion=true only if a free-credit/trial/promo is covered; worth_installing=true only if a tool worth installing is covered; promotions_found=true only if the deals section lists at least one real promotion or time-bound deal; top_deal = exact short name of the single best deal, or \"\".\n\nOUTPUT in this exact order:\n\nFirst: a JSON block with ALL of the fields below \u2014 never omit or drop a field; booleans are true ONLY when the body supports them:\n```json\n{\n  \"summary\": \"5-8 sentence executive summary covering the day\'s key stories, with the top deal highlighted\",\n  \"category\": [\"Open Source\", \"Frontier Models\"],\n  \"topics\": [\"AI Agents\"],\n  \"providers\": [\"OpenAI\"],\n  \"featured_models\": [\"GPT-5\"],\n  \"importance\": \"Medium\",\n  \"new_model_released\": false,\n  \"pricing_changed\": false,\n  \"open_source\": false,\n  \"free_promotion\": false,\n  \"worth_installing\": false,\n  \"best_coding_model\": \"\",\n  \"best_reasoning_model\": \"\",\n  \"best_local_model\": \"\",\n  \"best_value_api\": \"\",\n  \"biggest_release\": \"\",\n  \"promotions_found\": false,\n  \"top_deal\": \"\"\n}```\n\nThen the 10-section report:\n## Executive Summary\nWrite 5-8 sentences covering the most important stories of the day. Name specific models, companies, and numbers. Mention the top deal or promotion if one exists. Do NOT write a single vague sentence.\n## New Model Releases\n## Pricing & API Changes\n## Open Source Updates\n## AI Agent & MCP News\n## Coding Tools\n## \uD83D\uDD25 AI Deals, Pricing & Launch Intelligence\n\nPURPOSE: This section is NOT for reporting every AI news story. Its ONLY purpose is to make sure the reader NEVER misses: new model launches, launch discounts, introductory pricing, free credits, promotional usage multipliers, limited-time trials, subscription changes, new coding models, new API credits, student/startup offers, enterprise promotions, price reductions, off-peak pricing, early access programs, beta programs. Prioritize opportunities that SAVE MONEY or provide access to frontier models.\n\nMONITORED \u2014 Priority-1 platforms (coding platforms): Cursor, Qoder, OpenCode, Claude Code, OpenAI/Codex, Google AI Studio, Windsurf, Kiro, GitHub Copilot, Amazon Q Developer. Priority-2 providers (model providers): OpenAI, Anthropic, Google DeepMind, Qwen/Alibaba, QwenCloud, Z.ai, DeepSeek, Moonshot AI (Kimi), MiniMax, xAI, Mistral, Cohere. When the deals data is empty, do not invent \u2014 only report what is in DEALS & LAUNCH INTELLIGENCE DATA. Only report items from official blogs, changelogs, release notes, docs, forums, Discord announcements, official X/Twitter, GitHub releases. Never rely on unofficial rumors unless clearly labeled as rumor.\n\nFRESHNESS GATE \u2014 Before listing any item as a deal, check its date: if it is older than 14 days before TODAY\'S DATE and is not still active (End Date in the future), DROP it. In particular, never surface 2024/2025-era marketing posts (e.g. \"Introducing OpenAI for Nonprofits\") as today\'s deals just because they mention a discount keyword. Only genuinely fresh or currently time-bound offers belong here.\n\nDETECT \u2014 flag immediately if any appears: \"90% Off\", \"95% Off\", \"98% Off\", \"99% Off\", \"Launch Promotion\", \"Limited Time\", \"Free Credits\", \"Credits Multiplier\", \"Token Multiplier\", \"Bonus Credits\", \"Preview Pricing\", \"Beta Pricing\", \"Early Access\", \"Free Trial\", \"Extended Trial\", \"Student\", \"Startup\", \"Enterprise Credits\", \"Discount\", \"Coupon\", \"Promo\", \"Resource Pack\", \"Price Drop\", \"Price Reduction\", \"Usage Multiplier\", \"Off Peak\", \"Night Pricing\", \"Happy Hours\", \"Weekend Pricing\".\n\nFOR EVERY promotion report output a compact card (use bullet sub-lines under each promo, no markdown tables in body \u2014 Node 7\'s parser only handles headings/bullets/paragraphs/quote/divider):\n- Company | Product | Model | Promotion | Original Price | Discounted Price | Percentage Saved | Eligible Plans | Countries | Start Date | End Date | Remaining Days | Automatic? | Coupon Required? | Can stack with other offers? | Official link (use the actual official URL from the supplied data when available; if unavailable write \"Unknown\"; never invent one) | My action required | Priority (Critical/High/Medium/Low)\nIf a field is unknown write \"Unknown\" \u2014 NEVER invent prices or dates.\n\nSPECIAL RULES: If a promotion expires within 7 days mark it `\u{1F6A8} EXPIRING SOON`. If it expires within 48 hours mark it `\u{1F525} LAST CHANCE`. Compute \"Remaining Days\" from the End Date vs TODAY\'S DATE given at the top of the prompt.\n\nALSO DETECT (report as \"Launch & Product Intelligence\" sub-bullets, not promo cards): new frontier coding models, new preview models, new reasoning models, new coding benchmarks, new context windows, new agent products, new IDE integrations. Launch items MUST ALSO be merged into the matching report section (New Model Releases / Pricing & API Changes / Open Source Updates / Coding Tools) \u2014 mention once per section, never duplicate.\n\nFINAL SUMMARY at the end of the section, exactly this structure:\n- Top Money Saving Opportunity Today: <specific deal WITH actual numbers/prices and remaining time, e.g. \"Qwen Pro 50% off \u2014 $10 \u2192 $5 per 1M tokens \u2014 10 days left\">\n- Estimated Savings: <$ amount or Unknown>\n- Recommendation: <short actionable advice>\n- Should I switch today? Yes / No \u2014 Reason: <one line>\nIf no active promotion or time-bound deal exists, write exactly: \"Top Money Saving Opportunity Today: Nothing time-sensitive today.\" and do not invent one.\n\nFALLBACK: If nothing new exists today (no promotions and no launches detected), write exactly this single line instead of the whole section: \"No significant discounts or launch promotions detected today.\" Do NOT generate filler.\n\n## Notable Research\nList every AI-relevant item from RESEARCH DATA that is fresher than 14 days. Each item gets one bullet with title, one-line summary, and source URL. Skip non-AI items entirely.\n\n## Recommendations\nProvide 5-8 specific, actionable recommendations based on today\'s data. Each recommendation should reference a specific model, tool, or deal from the report. Format: \"- **Action** \u2014 why and how.\" Do NOT write fewer than 5 recommendations.\n\n## Sources\n\nThen paste the PRICING SECTION verbatim at the very end.';


// ── API call with model fallback ──────────────────────────────────
const apiKey = $env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY;
if (!apiKey) throw new Error('OPENROUTER_API_KEY is missing from environment');

const callModel = (model, reasoningEnabled) => this.helpers.httpRequest({
  method: 'POST',
  url: 'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions',
  headers: {
    'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + apiKey,
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
